  <main>
    <div class="grid">
      <section>
        <h2>Ingredients</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>30–50g Dutch Processed cocoa powder, plus more for dusting</li>
          <li>240g brewed espresso</li>
          <li>1 tablespoon vanilla extract</li>
          <li>5 large egg yolks</li>
          <li>100g white sugar</li>
          <li>¼ teaspoon salt</li>
          <li>250g mascarpone cheese, chilled (1 packet)</li>
          <li>420g heavy cream, chilled (2 packets)</li>
          <li>28 hard ladyfinger cookies</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Instructions</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Whisk together the cocoa powder, espresso, and vanilla in a bowl and set aside.</li>
          <li>In a mixer or using a hand mixer, beat the egg yolks and sugar until pale and thick, about 5 minutes.</li>
          <li>Add the salt and mascarpone cheese, and continue to whip until smooth.</li>
          <li>Add the chilled heavy cream and continue to whip until light, creamy, smooth, and able to hold a soft
            peak.</li>
          <li>Dunk each ladyfinger in the espresso mixture to absorb the liquid and start to line a 7x11 oval baking
            dish with the cookies. Quick 1-2 second dunking is enough.</li>
          <li>Top the first layer of cookies with ½ of the whipped mascarpone mixture and use the back of a metal spoon
            to spread it evenly.</li>
          <li>Dust with cocoa powder.</li>
          <li>Repeat for another layer, then finish by dusting with cocoa powder on top.</li>
          <li>Cover with plastic wrap and chill for at least 2 hours before serving.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>
